  "rustc": "rustc 1.98.1 (48a229cea 2026-09-01)\nbinary: rustc\ncommit-hash: 48a229ceaefd4985c50990b14116b6d856af0985\ncommit-date: 2026-09-01\nhost: x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu\nrelease: 1.98.1\nLLVM version: 22.1.8\n",
  "conditions": "Five sequential fresh processes and one full fixture run pinned to CPU 0 after every build/test exits. Region rows measure the operation plus checked result bounds, using fixed warm inputs and new PCB output wrappers; internal native-kernel evidence may already be warm. Input construction, first/last exact area and report-coordinate fingerprint checks are outside query timers but inside process RSS. Classification, bounds, area and emptiness rows each time one checked query; native handoff times a wrapper clone plus checked consuming export. Single/mixed aggregation and replacement rows also query checked result bounds. Fourteen witness rows and serialized bytes are identical across all five trials. The full two-board and Gerber fixture workload and its 120-second gate are unchanged."
